 West Broadway","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/AdvancedEquitiesPlazaSanDiegoApr09.jpg/960px-AdvancedEquitiesPlazaSanDiegoApr09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"One America Plaza","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.716244,"lo":-117.168712,"d":495,"ds":"One America Plaza is the tallest building in San Diego, California, and a prominent fixture in the waterfront district of the downtown San Diego skyline. The 34-story, 500 ft (150 m), 623,000 sq ft (57,900 m2), obelisk-shaped tower was designed by Helmut Jahn of Murphy/Jahn Architects and KMA Architecture.","wpu":"One America Plaza","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/OneAmericaPlazaSDSept10.jpg/960px-OneAmericaPlazaSDSept10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sapphire Tower (San Diego)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.719175,"lo":-117.169225,"d":569,"ds":"Sapphire Tower is a building in San Diego, California, and is a prominent fixture in San Diego's skyline. It has a height of 380 ft (116 m) and contains 97 units.","wpu":"Sapphire Tower (San Diego)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/SapphireTowerRearSanDiegoApr09.jpg/960px-SapphireTowerRearSanDiegoApr09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ruocco Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.711,"lo":-117.172,"d":586,"ds":"Ruocco Park is a park in San Diego, California. The 3.3-acre park overlooks San Diego Bay. The park features a public artwork, \"The Riparium,\" a sculptural gateway of eucalyptus tree branches designed by local artist Roman de Salvo.","wpu":"Ruocco Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/San_Diego%2C_2016_-_259.jpg/960px-San_Diego%2C_2016_-_259.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Guardian of Water","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.72196,"lo":-117.17269,"d":673,"ds":"Guardian of Water is a 1939 fountain and sculpture by Donal Hord, installed outside the San Diego County Administration Center, in the U.S. state of California. The statue was dedicated on June 10, 1939. In 1960, a replica of the fountain and sculpture was sent as a gift to San Diego's sister city of Yokohama by the San Diego-Yokohama Friendship Commission.","wpu":"Guardian of Water","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/Donal-Hord--9Guardian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Anthology (music venue)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.719494,"lo":-117.168103,"d":674,"ds":"Anthology was a 13,000 square foot, 325-seat live music venue and fine dining restaurant located at the south end of the Little Italy neighborhood of San Diego, California. It opened in summer 2007 and captured a modern feel of supper clubs of the 1930s and 40s in downtown San Diego.","wpu":"Anthology (music venue)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9a/Antholog_-_Main_Floor_%28W._Rail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Seaport Village Carousel","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.7095,"lo":-117.1714,"d":762,"ds":"The Seaport Village Carousel, also known as the Fair Park Looff Carousel, is a historic wooden carousel in the western wing of Seaport Village in San Diego, California. It was built by noted carver Charles I. D. Looff, who also constructed the Santa Monica Pier. The carousel costs a small fee to ride and contains 54 animals and 2 chariots.","wpu":"Seaport Village Carousel","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Seaport_Village_-_Fair_Park_Looff_Carousel%2C_built_in_1895_in_Brooklyn_NY.jpg/960px-Seaport_Village_-_Fair_Park_Looff_Carousel%2C_built_in_1895_in_Brooklyn_NY.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"110 Plaza","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.719304,"lo":-117.164399,"d":970,"ds":"110 Plaza, also known as the Commonwealth Building or the 110 Tower Building, is a 266 feet (81 m) modernist office building in downtown San Diego, Civic / Core Neighborhood. The address of the building is 110 West A Street, San Diego, CA 92101 and it is bordered by Front Street, A Street, 1st Avenue, and Ash Street. When the building opened in 1971, it was the first all-glass high rise in San Diego.","wpu":"110 Plaza","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e1/110_Plaza_Building.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Tower 180","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.716,"lo":-117.1631,"d":1019,"ds":"Tower 180, formerly the Executive Complex, is a 25-story building located at 180 Broadway in San Diego, California, United States. Upon completion in 1963, the 106.68 m (350.0 ft) building was the tallest in the city until 1969.","wpu":"Tower 180","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/ExecutiveComplexSanDiegoApr09.jpg/960px-ExecutiveComplexSanDiegoApr09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"San Diego Civic Theatre","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.717222,"lo":-117.1625,"d":1084,"ds":"The San Diego Civic Theatre is a performing arts venue in downtown San Diego, California. It opened in 1965. It is the performing home of the San Diego Opera and hosts other entertainment events such as concerts and musicals.","wpu":"San Diego Civic Theatre","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/34/SanDiegoCivicTheater_%28Opera_House%29_January_2010.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Amici Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.72311,"lo":-117.166055,"d":1085,"ds":"Amici Park is a park in Little Italy, San Diego. The park contains multiples bocce ball courts, a small amphitheater and a large playing field. The park is used by students of Washington Elementary School.","wpu":"Amici Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Amici_Park.jpg/960px-Amici_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Embarcadero Marina Park North","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.707,"lo":-117.169,"d":1104,"ds":"Embarcadero Marina Park North is a park in San Diego, California. It features Donal Hord's 1956 sculpture Morning.","wpu":"Embarcadero Marina Park North","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/San_Diego%2C_2016_-_273.jpg/960px-San_Diego%2C_2016_-_273.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Horton Plaza (shopping mall)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.713611,"lo":-117.1625,"d":1108,"ds":"Horton Plaza was a five-level outdoor shopping mall in downtown San Diego, California. It was designed by Jon Jerde and was known for its bright colors, architectural tricks, and odd spatial rhythms, occupying 6.5 city blocks adjacent to the city's historic Gaslamp Quarter. Opening in 1985, it was the first successful downtown retail center since the rise of suburban shopping centers decades earlier.","wpu":"Horton Plaza (shopping mall)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Hortonplazaarchitecture.jpg/960px-Hortonplazaarchitecture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"San Diego ( SAN dee-AY-goh; Spanish: [san ˈdjeɣo]) is a city on the Pacific coast of Southern California, next to the Mexican border. It is the eighth-most populous city in the U.S. and second-most populous city in California with a population of over 1.4 million, while the San Diego area with over 3.3 million residents is the 18th-largest metropolitan area in the country. San Diego is the county seat of San Diego County.","wpu":"San Diego","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/La_Jolla_Shores_view_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-La_Jolla_Shores_view_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}